Changes:
* November 2021: Rajbir Singh (Labour) resigns from council; seat left vacant until 2022 election<ref>{{cite news |last1=Storer |first1=Rhi |title=Rajbir Singh steps down as Sandwell councillor |url=https://www.halesowennews.co.uk/news/19726585.rajbir-singh-steps-sandwell-councillor/ |access-date=16 April 2022 |work=Halesowen News |date=18 November 2021 |language=en}}</ref>
* January 2022: Ian Chambers joins Labour from the Conservatives<ref>{{cite news |last1=Storer |first1=Rhi |title=Sandwell Conservative councillor defects to Labour |url=https://www.birminghammail.co.uk/news/sandwell-conservative-councillor-defects-labour-22812144 |access-date=16 April 2022 |work=BirminghamLive |date=20 January 2022 |language=en}}</ref>
* April 2022: Iqbal Singh Padda joins Conservatives from Labour<ref>{{cite news |last1=Madeley |first1=Peter |title=More chaos in Sandwell as Labour cabinet member quits party to stand for Tories |url=https://www.expressandstar.com/news/politics/2022/04/05/more-chaos-in-sandwell-as-labour-cabinet-member-quits-party-to-stand-for-tories/ |access-date=16 April 2022 |work=Express and Star |date=5 April 2022}}</ref>
* Independent councillors Yvonne Davies and Joanne Hadley form Sandwell Together<ref>{{cite web |title=Councillors by Party: Sandwell Together party {{!}} Sandwell Council |url=https://www.sandwell.gov.uk/councillors/specificParty/14/sandwell_together_party |website=www.sandwell.gov.uk |access-date=16 April 2022}}</ref>

